  "configuration_id": "config_006",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most informative first experiment is to test the 'full-featured' multimodal hypothesis: combining RNA (scvi_n200, a learned deep representation) and image (imagenet_vit_l, the strongest available encoder) modalities with multiprofile data, transformer aggregation (most flexible for capturing cell-cell interactions), and weighted fusion (learned modality importance). This configuration sits at the intersection of the most promising choices across all design dimensions. If it performs well, it establishes a strong upper-bound reference and subsequent experiments can ablate individual components (encoder choice, aggregation, fusion) to identify what drives performance. If it underperforms, it signals that complexity or a specific component is the bottleneck, guiding simplification in later experiments. Testing this 'best-guess' configuration first maximizes information gain per experiment under the tight 10-experiment budget, as it simultaneously validates the multimodal approach, the multiprofile setting, and the most powerful encoders/architecture in a single data point."
}

